696	                {c.detail}
697	              </p>
698	            </div>
699	          ))}
700	
701	          {/* Printing the nameservers is the point, not decoration: it is how the
702	              customer (or support) can tell this answer came from the zone's own
703	              authority and not from a stale recursive cache. */}
704	          <p className="text-[11px] text-slate-500">
705	            {report.nameservers.length > 0 ? (
706	              <>
707	                Read directly from this domain&apos;s nameservers (
708	                <span className="font-mono">{report.nameservers.join(", ")}</span>), so a record you
709	                just changed shows up straight away.
710	              </>
711	            ) : (
712	              <>Couldn&apos;t reach this domain&apos;s nameservers, so no record could be read.</>
713	            )}{" "}
714	            Checked {new Date(report.checkedAt).toLocaleTimeString()}.
715	          </p>
716	        </div>
717	      )}
718	    </div>
719	  );
720	}
